+# Area 52 fixed-pool recruitment
+
+This reuses the existing Playerbots recruiter, group invitation, teleport, duel and leave handlers. No addon or new client interface is required. The server changes must be deployed before using this flow.
+
+## Player use
+
+Outside combat and instances, at level 15–80, type `.playerbots coa tank`, `.playerbots coa heal`, or `.playerbots coa dps`. Alternatively, say `lfg bot tank`, `lfg bot heal`, or `lfg bot dps` in a configured recruitment channel (Zone or Newcomers by default). Be the party leader, leave Dungeon Finder queues, and have a party slot available.
+
+The server reserves a same-faction, uncommitted bot from the existing twenty. It prepares that bot at your exact level using the dungeon pool's existing build preparation. Wait for its ready whisper, then invite it normally within the two-minute reservation. The bot joins, follows and summons to you. A failed summon requests group departure rather than reporting success.
+
+Use the normal Duel action against your recruited bot. Only its controlling party member can initiate this pilot duel flow; dungeon queues, proposals, dungeon instances and reservations remain protected. Existing duel combat strategies and the controlling-player health exception remain in use. Finishing a duel does not automatically dismiss the bot. Whisper `leave` or remove it from the party when finished. After normal group removal, existing AI cleanup releases its controller and it becomes eligible for reuse when otherwise available.
+
+The pilot never creates additional characters to satisfy recruitment. It never changes assigned roles or falls back to generic CoA specialization rebuilding. Unavailable roles report unavailable. Expired offers release automatically. Changes to the requester's level or eligibility invalidate preparation/invitation. Recruitment and Dungeon Finder reservations exclude one another.
+
+## Equipment
+
+Fixed-pilot Heroes receive the owner's exact archetype equipment. Hoplite uses Hopstrike's reference set; Mystic Knight uses Mktest's. Naturalist uses Preened Ironfeather armor/cloak, two Rings of the Seer, Pendant of the Sorcerer, Paladin Libram of Healing, Dignified Headmaster's Charge, Swift Hand of Justice and Stick on a Carrot. The native item system scales these heirlooms with level.
+
+Matching item instances are retained through level changes and generic re-gearing. Assigned items are protected during inventory cleanup; if moved into bags they are re-equipped rather than duplicated. Exact initial assignment checks native equip legality and retries missing/temporarily unavailable slots without substituting other gear. Native Hero proficiencies permit Mystic Knight's selected mace; the old generic sword preference does not select fixed-profile gear.
+
+Primary Vanity sets use the existing collection appearance system: Mystic Knight900527, Naturalist900501 and Hoplite900573. These include armor and the set's weapon appearances; they do not replace functional items. Startup waits for collection data/state and retries when ready. Identical state does not produce repeated saves. No new item records or client addon are introduced.
+
+## Verification boundaries
+
+Offline checks exercise production recruitment/offer preparation, invitation/summon dispatch, duel admission, leave authorization and controller cleanup, plus dungeon contention and level transitions. External session, teleport and combat services are bounded adapters; their in-game acceptance remains with testers. Deployed item records and native DBC layouts/scaling functions qualify the allowed heirlooms across levels 15–80. Native build/unit checks cover integration. No gameplay environment or live announcement is run by this work.
